<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 3: </span>Statistical significance analysis of performance improvements between
GIER initial and final iteration outputs. Wilcoxon <math id="A3.T3.m39" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>-values indicate
whether per-sample changes are significant. Mean <math id="A3.T3.m40" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> reflects the
average improvement (or decline) from initial to final iteration.
The bootstrap CI indicates the range in which this average difference
likely lies. Results are from the GPT-4.1 model.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Prompts</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figures <a href="#A10.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ J.3 e-SNLI ‣ Appendix J Qualitative Examples ‣ GIER: Gap-Driven Self-Refinement for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, <a href="#A10.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ J.3 e-SNLI ‣ Appendix J Qualitative Examples ‣ GIER: Gap-Driven Self-Refinement for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, and <a href="#A10.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ J.3 e-SNLI ‣ Appendix J Qualitative Examples ‣ GIER: Gap-Driven Self-Refinement for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> show the GIER initial prompt used for the three tasks. Figures <a href="#A10.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ J.3 e-SNLI ‣ Appendix J Qualitative Examples ‣ GIER: Gap-Driven Self-Refinement for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>, <a href="#A10.F8" title="Figure 8 ‣ J.3 e-SNLI ‣ Appendix J Qualitative Examples ‣ GIER: Gap-Driven Self-Refinement for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>, and <a href="#A10.F9" title="Figure 9 ‣ J.3 e-SNLI ‣ Appendix J Qualitative Examples ‣ GIER: Gap-Driven Self-Refinement for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> show the GIER revision prompt used for the three tasks. The highest input token size of 20,296 appears in iteration 5 for PrivacyQA, but is within the context window length of all models. Similarly, output token sizes are also within all model limits.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.T4" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A4.T4.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A4.T4.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
